# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows but its stack runs on Linux (Docker, GitHub Actions). Without
# this file, `core.autocrlf` checks files out with CRLF, and a shell script with CRLF fails inside a
# container with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` — silently, on a fresh clone, not on the machine
# that authored it.
#
# Deliberately targeted rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf`: normalising every file would
# rewrite the whole working tree on the next checkout. Only the files that actually break, plus the
# ones consumed by Linux tooling, are pinned.

# Files executed or parsed inside Linux containers — CRLF breaks these.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf

# Consumed by Keycloak and the OTel collector inside containers.
*.json          text eol=lf

# C# and project files follow platform convention.
*.cs            text
*.csproj        text
*.props         text
*.targets       text
*.sln           text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.nupkg         binary
*.dll           binary
